 ("How do I tell if I have the 5 ft or 6 ft bed?",
  "XtraCab trucks only come with the 6 ft bed. Double Cabs come with either. Retailers list the short bed as 5' (60 in). The long bed appears as 6' (72 in) on BAK's listing and 6' (74 in) on Tyger's, and one Tacoma4G owner measured 73.5 in along the floor of a 6 ft TRD Off-Road bed. To check, measure inside the bed from the front wall to the closed tailgate. About 60 in means the 5 ft bed, and anything past 70 in is the 6 ft."),
 ("Why does the Amazon listing say 2024–2025 when I have a 2026?",
  "Listing titles often lag the model year. The Amazon titles for the Extang Solid Fold ALX 88832, Extang Trifecta ALX 90832 and TruXedo Lo Pro 556101 say 2024–2025, while RealTruck's product pages list the same part numbers for 2024–2026. The Tyger T3 title says 2024–2025, but Tyger's own page says 24–26. Match the part number, then confirm the year on the listing or with the seller."),
 ("Can I keep using the deck rail cleats with a cover on?",
  "Usually, but with less room. Owners on Tacoma4G report that the Extang Solid Fold ALX only uses small sections of the factory tracks, that BAK covers leave room to reach the tie-downs, and that Toyota's own cover sits its brackets behind the rails. Most covers here clamp to the rail system, so a cleat may have to move away from the clamp points. Check the install sheet for the cover you're buying."),
 ("Which cover has the highest load rating on a 2024+ Tacoma?",
  "The Extang Solid Fold ALX, at 600 lb evenly distributed, from 1 in thick EnduraShield TPO panels on an aluminum frame. RealTruck lists the RetraxPRO EZ-Off at over 500 lb, and the BAKFlip MX4 at 400 lb. The soft covers (TruXedo Lo Pro, Extang Trifecta ALX, Tyger T3) are vinyl and carry no rating. Ratings assume the load is spread flat. A knee or a sharp corner on one spot can still damage a panel."),
 ("Are there fewer cover choices for the 6 ft bed?",
  "In what we found, yes. Of the covers here, the only 2024+ 6 ft listings with part numbers in the title were the BAKFlip MX4 448447 and the Tyger T3 TG-BC3T1202. Most launch-era listings target the 5 ft Double Cab, which is the more common setup. If you have an XtraCab or a 6 ft Double Cab, ask the brand for its 6 ft part number and check that the listing says 6 ft."),
